From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 02:03:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: end a reply stream where the guest declared it

vkr_cs_encoder_set_stream_locked() validates the offset and size the guest
passes through vkSetReplyCommandStreamMESA, stores them, and then sets the
encoder's end pointer to the end of the whole shared-memory resource.
Every write bound -- vkr_cs_encoder_write() and the raw pointer handed out
by vkr_cs_encoder_get_blob_storage() -- is computed from that pointer, so a
reply larger than the window the guest declared was accepted and written
past it, silently, into whatever else the guest keeps in that resource.

End the stream at offset + size, which the function has already proven is
inside the resource.  An oversized reply now marks the context fatal where
it used to overrun.
---
 src/venus/vkr_cs.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_cs.c b/src/venus/vkr_cs.c
index 4e4f9b08f1f2b29c05ad892ee9bd713322774d52..6d48bfb35448197650a542fcd7dd0baa3648acb7 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_cs.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_cs.c
@@ -32,7 +32,12 @@ vkr_cs_encoder_set_stream_locked(struct vkr_cs_encoder *enc,
    enc->stream.offset = offset;
    enc->stream.size = size;
 
-   enc->end = res->u.data + res->size;
+   /* Every write bound is computed from enc->end, so it has to end the window
+    * the guest declared rather than the resource that happens to hold it.  A
+    * reply the guest sized for one command could otherwise run on through
+    * whatever else the guest keeps in the same shared-memory resource.
+    */
+   enc->end = res->u.data + offset + size;
 
    vkr_cs_encoder_seek_stream_locked(enc, 0);
 }
